    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nThe preview window sometimes opens with a non-zero column position, so the beginning of the file content is not visible.\n\nExpected behavior:\nThe preview should always start at column 0 when displaying a file.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. create 'init.lua' and populate it with the following content:\n\n    ```lua\n    vim.pack.add({ \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\" })\n\n    vim.g.mapleader = ' ' -- Use `<Space>` as <Leader> key\n\n    require(\"mini.files\").setup({ windows = { preview = true } })\n\n    local nmap_leader = function(suffix, rhs, desc)\n\t    vim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<Leader>\" .. suffix, rhs, { desc = desc })\n    end\n\n    local explore_at_file = \"<Cmd>lua MiniFiles.open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0))<CR>\"\n\n    nmap_leader(\"ef\", explore_at_file, \"File directory\")\n    ```\n\n3. Open a C++ file using `nvim *.cpp`, then press `<Leader>ef`. The preview window starts at a non-zero column position. Press `q` to exit, then press `<Leader>ef` again. The previously previewed file now starts at column 0, while an unpreviewed file still starts at a non-zero colum. The behavior is demonstrated in the attached video.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6ede0ec3-6587-4620-acce-5b04267cc2e1",
