            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI can reproduce using the [llvm](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project) project as shown in the video.\nIf the first line starts a comment and ends with '//', the problem occurs. \nFor example, `clang/include/clang/Options/Options.h\n\n```txt\n//===--- Options.h - Option info & table ------------------------*- C++ -*-===//\n```\n\nIf I remove the last '//', or when I add an empty line above, preview succeeds.\n\nEDIT: Also happens when the line ends with a single `/`\nEDIT: The [problem](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/9459d7f41ae77d909579dab0aea2bdd3210fac9f/lua/mini/files.lua#L2610): Because of the '/', the cursor is tweaked, and changes from {1,0} to {1, 79}",
